  "column_map_note": "MAPPED TO THE SERVER'S HEADER, WHICH DOES NOT MATCH ITS OWN DATA. motor_ai_server writes the columns in the same order as the training recordings (timestamp, I1..I3, speed_cmd, V1..V3, vdc, ax, ay, az) but emits a header that names them in a different order, so the column after the currents is labelled Volt_0 while it carries the speed command, and the one labelled Speed_volt_cmd carries the DC bus. Verified 2026-08-21 on a live 26000-row window: relabelled in training order all 8 electrical columns match the rig profile, and the column the header calls Speed_volt_cmd is steady at 2633 +- 13 which is a DC bus, not a command. Currents are unaffected either way -- they occupy the same positions in both orders -- which is why the anomaly stage (4 balance features, current only) was correct on the device while classification and RUL, which need PF/Z from the voltages, were fed the speed command as a phase voltage. THIS MAPPING IS A COMPENSATION FOR THAT BUG. If the server is ever corrected to emit a truthful header, this file must be reverted to the training order or the node breaks in exactly the same way, silently. The training-order map is kept below as column_map_training_order.",
